WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.460
Hey team it’s Charlie, this week for my
bonus video I reached into the mailbag since

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.590
I haven’t done a Game of Thrones Q&amp;A in
a couple weeks.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.741
There’s also been a few important things
going on with the show lately so a few of

00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:14.410
the questions get into that but I’ll also
have some announcements at the end of the

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.410
video.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.829
Now to questions, careful for spoilers for
everything through season 4.

00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:22.289
So let’s get going

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:28.779
Question 1 - igo 170 asks do you think World
of Ice and Fire will be out of date when Martin

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:31.189
publishes the rest of the books?

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:37.320
There’s a lot of things that aren’t going
to be in there but the book is mostly intended

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.140
to be additive material that the future novels
won’t cover in depth.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.140
It’s not going to get into the life story
for all the characters in the novels.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.140
He’s written a lot of new things for it.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.140
Not full chapters but snippets of history.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.140
The preview he released of Aegon the Conqueror
is a good example.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.740
He’ll have things like that in the book.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.210
It’s not going to be a summary of everything
that’s going on right now.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.650
So yes, there will be a lot of new things
happening after it’s published, but it was

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.980
never going to be a complete history of everyone
and everything.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.010
I haven’t seen the table of contents yet,
but think of world of ice and fire as being

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.940
like the book of maps they released.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.120
Lands of Ice and Fire combined with some extra
historical information about some of the families

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.360
and places.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.620
There are complete family trees for the starks
and the targaryens.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.320
The way they said it made me think they only
did those two families, but without a table

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.140
of contents I can’t confirm that.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:21.070
The book is out tuesday October 28th so I
might give a few copies away that week.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:24.580
There is a kindle edition but I also pre-ordered
the hardback.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:30.990
It’s going to be a beautiful book, so if
you were ever going to buy the physical book,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.990
this would be a good time.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:38.450
Question 2 - Marzie asks why did Daenerys
say that Viserys wasn’t a true dragon.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.090
If fire can’t hurt dragons does that mean
he wasn’t a Targaryen?

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.950
That’s actually a misconception.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:02:02.450
Targaryens can totally be burned by fire 
when magic is not involved.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.150
Wildfire is particularly deadly to them.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.860
Especially when they try to eat it.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:12.620
It’s one of the things the books and the
show haven’t fully explained, but it gets

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.620
into magic.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.970
When Daenerys sits in Khal Drogo’s fire
and emerges unburnt it could have been blood

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.610
magic, which sounds a lot like the magic the
Valyrians practiced.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.990
The show also called the burning of the leeches
in season 3 blood magic, so it could also

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.940
be related to the magic of the red god.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.380
Or it could be a completely unrelated type
of magic.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:33.680
I don’t totally expect the books to spell
it out, but that’s where additive books

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.300
like World of Ice and Fire come in.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.720
Martin will probably continue to support extra
books like that.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.020
The book itself was pioneered by the people
behind Westeros dot org and Martin just helped

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.020
out.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:49.170
It would be like someone writing a complete
history of the Time War for Doctor Who.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.710
That show will probably never fully do that
event, but it’s this big huge thing that

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.560
fans want to know about.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.090
So anytime people complain about Winds of
Winter, just remember how much new info we

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.980
get from those extra books.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.960
Question 3 - Navdaz asks Can you do a video
about the unexplored places in the world like

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.400
Sothoryos?

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.880
There are a couple of really big places the
books haven’t gone yet.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:25.480
And I say yet, because Martin has talked about
Flashbacks to Old Valyria before the doom

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.160
in future books.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:32.990
Sothoryos however you want to pronounce it,
is a good analog of Africa, just in the way

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:38.330
Daenerys describes it inhabitants and jungles
makes me think of the Amazon or sub saharan

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.190
Africa.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:44.819
Characters in the books have been there but
I don’t think there’s quite enough information

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:47.530
about that continent in particular to do a
whole video on.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:52.400
It’s way too big a mystery for Martin to
not go there in a future book.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.230
Winter is supposedly coming for everyone right?

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.470
So Winter would have to come to the Jungle
too.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:03.280
Until the books go there I’ll probably just
work those places into other videos when it’s

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.280
relevant.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:10.720
Question 4 - This Vik asks are the faith militant
a defence force or do they also attack certain

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.420
houses?

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:17.720
Their standing mission is to uphold the orders
of the High Septon.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:23.080
Or in the case of Season 5 the High Sparrow
if you want to use his nickname.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:27.300
In the past they’ve only gone after people
they think are violating morals of the faith.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.210
They’re like the censorship police.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.740
If you are doing something that they deem
unholy or ungodly they will meet you with

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.070
force and bring you before the High Septon
for judgement.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:41.320
Because we might see them in season 5, if
you have read the books please use spoiler

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.260
tags in the comments.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:51.070
Question 5 - Man I Hate wasp asks whos stories
are split in books four and five?

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:57.030
The books were split because Martin felt he
couldn’t fit all the POV characters into

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.030
one book.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.910
So the time period is the same for both books,

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:04.810
you just don’t hear from book 4 characters
in book 5 unless the characters in book 5

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.669
are thinking about book 4 characters.

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:12.770
The POV characters are a mixture of new characters
they just cast in season 5 like Hotah and

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.660
characters they cut out like Arys Oakheart
and Arianne Martell.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:19.740
Most of what happens in Book 4 will be season
5 of the show.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:24.250
But because Daenerys and Tyrion don’t really
appear in Book 4, season 5 will also get into

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:30.960
Book 5 stuff.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:35.840
Question 6 - Flame for Moonlight asks will
there be more Dragons in season 5?

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.470
Yes, lots more dragons.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:44.759
I feel like of all the possible CG things
the show could choose to do, the dragons are

00:05:44.759 --> 00:05:46.970
one of the first things they think about every
year.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:59.500
I feel like the producers and casual fans
of the show use dragons as a way to explain

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.470
what it’s about to other people.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:05.620
Like when someone who has never read the books
asks what’s game of thrones about?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.570
Another random person says Dragons and Ice
People.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:15.210
That’s a fraction of it, but it’s something
easy for non-hardcore people to latch on to.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:22.180
So there will always be dragons on the show.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:26.030
They’d be the last thing that would ever
get cut.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:30.620
Question 7 - Albert A asks, do you think they’d
ever freeze someone’s story from the books

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:31.880
for a whole season?

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:36.449
Not one of the big main characters.

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:42.580
Little characters like Gendry, Hodor and Lancel
yes, either they’d just not use them for

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:47.160
a season or they’d just drop them from the
story completely.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:59.020
Hodor is confirmed sitting out season 5 even
though Isaac Hemstead Wright has said he has

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:06.289
shot scenes for 
the premiere.

00:07:06.289 --> 00:07:10.949
When Martin talks about the show changing
more and more from the books over time, it’s

00:07:10.949 --> 00:07:17.259
because the show keeps using characters that
Martin hasn’t used

00:07:17.259 --> 00:07:21.169
and as a result it doesn’t have room to
bring in new characters that Martin brings

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:22.169
in.

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:28.980
Like Arianne Martell.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:34.360
Question 8 - Troll Kidd asks would HBO ever
fire one of the stars like Emilia Clarke if

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:37.240
they said a spoiler?

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.800
Not if they felt they were critical to the
ending they’d envisioned.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:50.210
And to be honest, I feel like all the hardcore
fans will have already imagined every possible

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.330
outcome for the show.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:08:14.770
Most of the people that watch the show don’t
search for extra information online, that’s

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:18.520
usually just the highly engaged part of the
fandom that really wants to talk about what’s

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:31.840
going on.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.180
Most people are just passive observers.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:39.089
Like they want HBO to wheel the dump truck
of content up to their house and leave.

00:08:39.089 --> 00:08:43.399
That’s slowly changing because of something
google calls generation C. It’s a way to

00:08:43.399 --> 00:08:49.000
describe the millenial, gen x, gen y crowd
that consume content primarily on digital

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:59.730
platforms.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.720
Those people, of which we are all a part are
much more likely to actively engage with shows,

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:07.130
search for information about it online and
engage in online conversations about in on

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.130
social media

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.170
like this youtube video.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:11.089
In the next 5 years, we will become the majority.

00:09:11.089 --> 00:09:13.769
But we’re not quite there yet.

00:09:13.769 --> 00:09:18.769
Question 9 - Dan Cummings asks, could you
do a video on what scenes they have been filming?

00:09:18.769 --> 00:09:23.770
Okay, since this could be potentially super
spoilery I’m going to put this tag up and

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:27.209
you can just skip till it goes away if you
want.

00:09:27.209 --> 00:09:28.259
I’ll wait just a sec...okay.

00:09:28.259 --> 00:09:34.569
They just started building the Winterfell
set again, so there will be lots of Winterfell

00:09:34.569 --> 00:09:35.569
scenes.

00:09:35.569 --> 00:09:38.329
Remember, the Boltons were marching there
during season 4.

00:09:38.329 --> 00:09:44.579
They also constructed sets for the House of
Black and White, the place where the faceless

00:09:44.579 --> 00:09:46.760
men are headquartered.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:52.149
They filmed near the cathedral in Dubrovnik
with Cersei, so they’re doing that big scene

00:09:52.149 --> 00:09:54.730
from Book 4.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:59.329
They filmed a river boat scene with Tyrion,
Varys and possibly Jorah Mormont.

00:09:59.329 --> 00:10:03.110
Mormont was described in the same post I saw
but he wasn’t pictured with Tyrion and Varys.

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:05.779
And none of them were actually filmed.

00:10:05.779 --> 00:10:21.519
It was just reported they were on set.

00:10:21.519 --> 00:10:27.290
And they’ve also filmed the fighting pits
of Meereen.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.959
This is what it looks like.

00:10:28.959 --> 00:10:33.050
Most of those scenes are for pretty major
things, so again, please use spoiler tags

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:35.100
if you want to talk more about them in the
comments.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:40.459
Okay spoilers over Question 10 - Juan Hunter
asks, how many seasons do you think the show

00:10:40.459 --> 00:10:43.180
will run and will they do prequel shows?

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:50.299
HBO seems pretty comfortable with 7 seasons
for less successful things like True Blood,

00:10:50.299 --> 00:10:53.000
so bare minimum 7.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:58.430
Game Of Thrones is by far their most popular
Drama since Sopranos, so they’ll try to

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:01.749
keep it going as long as the producers can
keep coming up with new stories.

00:11:01.749 --> 00:11:06.670
I think it will be season 6 before we see
how much they stretch the plot of the books

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:07.670
out.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.949
There’s no reason they couldn’t do 10
seasons, but I’m not expecting them to take

00:11:10.949 --> 00:11:11.949
it that far.

00:11:11.949 --> 00:11:12.949
As for prequels.

00:11:12.949 --> 00:11:17.069
George RR Martin signed a development deal
during season 1 for a separate show.

00:11:17.069 --> 00:11:21.500
There’s no word on what that will be other
than it will be a prequel and it will not

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.839
be from recent history.

00:11:22.839 --> 00:11:24.829
It’s not going to be a Robert’s Rebellion
prequel.

00:11:24.829 --> 00:11:32.059
It would more likely be from the time of the
Dance of The Dragons or during the reign of

00:11:32.059 --> 00:11:34.579
one of the crazier Targaryen Kings.

00:11:34.579 --> 00:11:37.769
Either way whenever it gets here I’ll continue
to support it.

00:11:37.769 --> 00:11:40.779
But thank you so much for submitting questions
everyone.

00:11:40.779 --> 00:11:46.430
I’ll try to post my next bonus video either
this friday or next friday.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:51.019
I’m trying to turn Fridays into my Game
of Thrones days but so many new things are

00:11:51.019 --> 00:11:53.290
coming I’ll just have to see how it goes.

